    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "***PRIME CITY CENTRE LOCATION / 2 BED 2 BATH / BALCONY / THIRD FLOOR / SECURE ACCESS / LIFT ACCESS / EXCELLENT TRANSPORT LINKS / CLOSE TO ENTERPRISE & BUSINESS OPPORTUNITIES***\r\n\r\nKELLY BRADSHAW  are truly delighted to offer a superb 2 bedroom 2 bathroom 3rd floor apartment to the sales market. \r\n\r\nDesigned by Laughton Tyler, “The Steelworks” has been put forward as an example of quality architecture in the city with Dublin's nomination for the European City of Urbanism award. Constructed to the highest standard in 2004, the mixed use development of residential, retail and office space surrounds an attractive internal courtyard.\r\n\r\nApartment 12 The Stockyard, The Steelworks, Foley Street, Dublin 1, a superb two bedroom apartment is presented to the market in fine condition throughout and is situated in an excellent central location, in the heart of Dublin City Centre.\r\n\r\nThe city pad is finished to a high standard where light prevails throughout. On entering the entrance hallway you are greeted by hardwood flooring, and two large storage closets, which have partial shelving and ample storage space, essential in any apartment. Off the hallway there are two large double bedrooms, with fitted wardrobes, the master which has an ensuite. Onto the large bright open/dining area, with floor to ceiling glazing & sliding patio doors you will be pleasantly surprised by the spacious and light flooded room. Off the living room is the fully fitted modern shaker style kitchen with floor and wall tiling. The accommodation is completed by the family bathroom, which is fully tiled and benefits from a bath and overhead shower.\r\n\r\nThe convenience of the location of this property cannot be overstated. The Steelworks is situated on Foley Street, a diverse multicultural melting pot, nestled between Talbot Street and Amiens Street opposite Connolly Station & Busaras with easy access to a host of essential amenities & transport links. O'Connell Street is just 1km walk away and the IFSC is just 800m walk making this an attractive opportunity for owner occupier first time buyers, investors or those in need of a city base in the heart of Dublin City Centre. Situated within the central business district, this area has seen major rejuvenation over the years with the completion of the International Financial Services Centre.\r\n\r\nThe area has become an established office location with Bord Gais taking offices adjacent to the Steelworks and Bank of Ireland Treasury offices at the junction with James Joyce Street. The new Independent House is likewise nearby. The development is a targeted site within the NEIC (North East Inner City) integrated area plan.\r\n\r\nThe developments location beside a host of entertainment, tourist, retail, business, educational & recreational amenities will appeal to all who view it.\r\n\r\nEarly viewing is therefore recommended to appreciate this property in its entirety and is available through Kelly Bradshaw on 018040500."
      },
